Revision history for Plack-Middleware-Zitadel

{{$NEXT}}
    - Ship a LICENSE file so the distribution builds again
    - Run the test suite on GitHub Actions
    - Repair the documentation: the POD parses again and lists SYNOPSIS,
      DESCRIPTION, ATTRIBUTES and SEE ALSO
    - Repair the README usage example: it enables Plack::Middleware::Zitadel
      instead of a class that does not exist, and a test now runs it
    - Escape the error text in the WWW-Authenticate challenge: quotes and
      backslashes are backslash-escaped, line breaks and other control
      characters can no longer reach the header (the JSON body is unchanged)
    - Answer 403 insufficient_scope with a WWW-Authenticate challenge that
      carries the realm and the required scopes in the scope attribute, as
      RFC 6750 describes; before, the 403 had no such header

0.010     2026-04-16 23:54:26Z
    - Initial release of Plack::Middleware::Zitadel:
      - Bearer token verification via WWW::Zitadel::OIDC
      - Optional audience verification
      - Optional required scope checks
      - Claims injection into PSGI env (`zitadel.claims`)
    - Test coverage for auth success/failure and scope enforcement
    - Transparent proxy PSGI example (`examples/proxy.psgi`)
    - Dockerfile for containerized middleware deployment
    - Kubernetes manifests + deploy script for Gateway API usage
